  message: "CORRECTION 2026-11-21 (audit revision agent, probe at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/audit/probe4_electron/RESULT.txt): this description's claim that electron.yaml 'already detects contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld as api_bridge' is false. The row exists but is decorator-keyed on a call, and js_ts writes meta.decorators only from @decorator syntax, so it never fires (same defect as the six dead entrypoint rows); nothing reads api_bridge. On the probe, preload.js and renderer.js are script_module entries, and linkers/ipc.py emits a calls edge with meta.bridge_kind=context_bridge from renderer.js to preload.js. The electron_preload producer must therefore come from a usage-keyed row (the shape of electron.yaml's working app.whenReady / app.on rows) or from the IPC linker's context-bridge detection, and the BrowserWindow webPreferences.preload path where it is a literal. The other call-keyed decorator rows in electron.yaml (ipc_handler, ipc_sender, window, lifecycle) have the same shape and were not each probed: sweep them in this item."  # 8ca6
